    {
      "path": "src/itg/d08p/d5/support.ts",
      "content": "This nests a second conditional expression inside the first, contrary to the checklist's prohibition on nested ternaries. Use explicit if/else branches for the card, Detail, and page cases so the selector scope is clear.",
      "suggestion_code": "  let form: Locator;\n  if (card !== undefined) {\n    form = await debtFormOf(page, card);\n  } else if (where === 'Detail') {\n    form = detail.debtForm(page);\n  } else {\n    form = debtForm(page);\n  }",
      "existing_code": "  const form = card !== undefined ? await debtFormOf(page, card) : where === 'Detail' ? detail.debtForm(page) : debtForm(page);",
      "start_line": 68,
      "end_line": 68,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/itg/d08p/d2/narrow.ts",
      "content": "This scenario opens only Plan and Risk before measuring every Detail table, including Open Lots in Position. Once drawers exist, Position's tables will either be absent (so the loop silently skips them) or hidden (so their zero-sized geometry passes). Open Position at each width and assert its tables are visible before measuring them; measure other table-bearing drawers separately to preserve the existing overflow coverage.",
      "existing_code": "      await expectReflowed(page, `resolved Open Detail at ${width}`, detail.TABLES);",
      "start_line": 86,
      "end_line": 86,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/itg/d08p/d2/ui-alignment.ts",
      "content": "Passing detail.CARDS only scopes the card lookup: lefts still reads the first page-wide tablist and heading. In particular, the Detail tablist that openDrawer supports will add a `tablist` key and fail this exact-key assertion even with correct layout. Move the Detail geometry reads into the scoped helper layer and distinguish drawer navigation from the Trades lifecycle tabs, rather than retaining the assumption that Detail has no tablist.",
      "existing_code": "    const openDetail = await lefts(detail.CARDS);\n    expect(Object.keys(openDetail).sort(), 'Open Detail elements').toEqual(['card', 'h1']);",
      "start_line": 378,
      "end_line": 379,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/itg/d08p/support/detail/position.ts",
      "content": "Scope this value to the Valuation card rather than the entire Detail. DatedSection also renders ValuationFigures, including another `Realized to date` term, whenever a dated line is present. In that state this locator resolves to two `dd` elements and the single-element assertions in the exit suites fail in strict mode. Using `valueIn(regionOf(page, 'Valuation'), 'Realized to date')` also satisfies the required card-scoping contract.",
      "suggestion_code": "export const realizedToDate = (page: Page): Locator =\u003e valueIn(regionOf(page, 'Valuation'), 'Realized to date');",
      "existing_code": "export const realizedToDate = (page: Page): Locator =\u003e valueIn(detailRoot(page), 'Realized to date');",
      "start_line": 19,
      "end_line": 19,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/itg/d08p/support/detail/index.ts",
      "content": "Wait for the Detail root to be attached before checking whether it has tabs. `count()` does not auto-wait, and several callers invoke this immediately after `page.goto()` or `page.reload()`, while TradeDetail initially renders a loading state without `.trade-detail`. Once the drawer shell exists, this can return during loading instead of selecting the requested drawer. Waiting for the root first still allows the current tabless layout to return without a click.",
      "existing_code": "  if ((await tabs.count()) === 0) return;",
      "start_line": 19,
      "end_line": 19,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/itg/d08p/d2/ui-alignment.ts",
      "content": "This still measures all Detail definition lists together rather than reading each card in its active drawer. In the capped-row test, only Plan and Risk or Position is opened at a time: lists in other drawers will either disappear from this query or return zero-sized rectangles, so oversized rows can pass unnoticed (and the aggregate row-count assertion can change with drawer mounting). Move these measurements into card-scoped support helpers and open the corresponding drawer before measuring each set of rows, preserving the existing width assertions.",
      "existing_code": "  detail.root(page).locator('dl:not(.answers)').evaluateAll((lists) =\u003e",
      "start_line": 1350,
      "end_line": 1350,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
